*> PLB-C095 rewrite-without-read: a sequential REWRITE or DELETE that
*> does not follow a READ of its file.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. NOREAD.
ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
FILE-CONTROL.
    SELECT SEQ-FILE ASSIGN TO "seq.dat" ORGANIZATION SEQUENTIAL
        FILE STATUS IS WS-FS.
    SELECT IDX-FILE ASSIGN TO "idx.dat" ORGANIZATION INDEXED
        ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC RECORD KEY IS IDX-KEY
        FILE STATUS IS WS-FS.
    SELECT KEY-FILE ASSIGN TO "key.dat" ORGANIZATION INDEXED
        ACCESS MODE IS SEQUENTIAL RECORD KEY IS KEY-KEY
        FILE STATUS IS WS-FS.
DATA DIVISION.
FILE SECTION.
FD  SEQ-FILE.
01  SEQ-REC             PIC X(10).
FD  IDX-FILE.
01  IDX-REC.
    05  IDX-KEY         PIC X(4).
    05  IDX-DATA        PIC X(6).
FD  KEY-FILE.
01  KEY-REC.
    05  KEY-KEY         PIC X(4).
    05  KEY-DATA        PIC X(6).
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01  WS-FS               PIC XX.
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
MAIN-LINE.
    *> Reported: after the OPEN, after a REWRITE, after a DELETE, and
    *> in the next sentence.
    OPEN I-O SEQ-FILE KEY-FILE IDX-FILE
    REWRITE SEQ-REC
    READ SEQ-FILE
    REWRITE SEQ-REC
    REWRITE SEQ-REC
    READ KEY-FILE
    DELETE KEY-FILE
    DELETE KEY-FILE
    READ SEQ-FILE.
    REWRITE SEQ-REC.
    REWRITE SEQ-REC.
    *> Not reported: after a READ, inside its NOT AT END, after a
    *> PERFORM, and with dynamic access (by key).
    READ SEQ-FILE
        NOT AT END
            REWRITE SEQ-REC
    END-READ
    READ SEQ-FILE
    REWRITE SEQ-REC
    PERFORM READ-NEXT
    REWRITE SEQ-REC
    MOVE "0001" TO IDX-KEY
    REWRITE IDX-REC
    DELETE IDX-FILE
    CLOSE SEQ-FILE KEY-FILE IDX-FILE
    STOP RUN.
READ-NEXT.
    READ SEQ-FILE.
